cant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AOKI, TOMOKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUO, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAHARA, TATSURO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TONEN CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AOKI TOMOKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUO HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAHARA TATSURO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AOKI, TOMOKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUO, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAHARA, TATSURO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A photosensitive polysilazane composition which is usable as a positive resist; and a method of forming a patterned polysilazane film from the composition. The composition is characterized by comprising a polysilazane, especially polymethylsilazane or polyphenylsilazane, and a photo-acid generator. A coating film of the photosensitive polysilazane composition is pattern-wise irradiated with light. The irradiated part is dissolved away to obtain a patterned polysilazane film.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de polysilazane photosensible laquelle peut être utilisée en tant que résist positif, et un procédé de formation d'une couche mince de polysilazane à motif à partir de la composition. La composition est caractérisée en ce qu'elle contient un polysilazane, notamment un polyméthylsilazane ou un polyphénylsilazane, et un générateur de photo-acide. Une couche mince de revêtement constituée de la composition de polysilazane photosensible est exposée côté motif à des rayons de lumière. La partie irradiée est éliminée par dissolution afin d'obtenir une couche mince de polysilazane à motif.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>